bee4f2","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/10/#testresult/120a99a2cebee4f2","status":"passed","time":{"start":1794002592000,"stop":1794003362670,"duration":770670}},{"uid":"cb85e753b9e43743","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/9/#testresult/cb85e753b9e43743","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793948341000,"stop":1793949105260,"duration":764260}},{"uid":"cb4096a1a4b3b212","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/8/#testresult/cb4096a1a4b3b212","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793832981000,"stop":1793833816860,"duration":835860}},{"uid":"20739522777101c1","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/6/#testresult/20739522777101c1","status":"failed","statusDetails":"failed to onboard device \"edge-dev1\": context deadline exceeded\n\nClaude's conclusion:\n### Root cause\n\nLive evidence shows `edge-dev1`'s Proxmox VM (126) was powered on cleanly alongside `edge-dev2`/`edge-dev3` (124/129, no VM-ID collision), and its console confirms the kernel booted and `containerd` started successfully by `23:12:08` — but boot then silently stalled: SDN's dnsmasq DHCP log shows `edge-dev2` and `edge-dev3` completing DHCPDISCOVER→DHCPACK at `23:12:20`/`23:12:31` and onboarding by `23:13:05`, while `edge-dev1`'s MAC (`26:9f:78:99:86:67`) never sent a single DHCP packet and never appears in `ip neigh` on the SDN at all. The SDN-side tap interface for `edge-dev1` does show `LOWER_UP`, confirming the vNIC was attached at the hypervisor level — so this is a guest-side early-boot hang (something between containerd startup and network bring-up never completed), not an SDN/broker networking problem, and `evetest status` still shows it stuck `EVE_DEVICE_STATE_UNDEFINED` with no interfaces at all ~10 minutes later. This does not share a root cause with the two other `TestNodeClusterSuite` failures already investigated in this run (`TestNativeKubeAppNetworking`'s apiserver-readiness race, `TestMgmtProxy`'s registry-routing bug) — both of those occur well after onboarding, whereas this device never got network at all. The exact \"failed to onboard device ... context deadline exceeded\" error string has occurred once before, on 2026-11-01 (run #4, `TestClusterPVCRedownload`), where one sibling VM silently never produced further boot output while others onboarded fine — that time attributed to the Proxmox host \"farfalle\" being under sustained TLS-handshake-timeout stress; tonight shows no such TLS-timeout signature from the broker, so while the general \"one concurrently-booted sibling VM silently stalls\" mechanism is recurring, it isn't confirmed to be driven by the same infrastructure cause, and no dedicated ledger entry exists yet for this specific pattern.","time":{"start":1793657001000,"stop":1793657865120,"duration":864120}},{"uid":"98681b1799361d52","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/5/#testresult/98681b1799361d52","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793573870000,"stop":1793575600360,"duration":1730360}},{"uid":"d3ee7b4e7fdaed3","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/4/#testresult/d3ee7b4e7fdaed3","status":"failed","statusDetails":"Failed","time":{"start":1793485364000,"stop":1793485725340,"duration":361340}}]},"tags":[]},"source":"89c67a68a56ab51f.json","parameterValues":[]}